      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-04T15:59:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although is that what the code is doing?  If the child has exited, shouldn\u0027t we always escape from the loop?  The success check seems to only repeat in the loop until timeout.",
      "parentUuid": "fb5c6279_9ad5d8cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 157,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "6a682ff8fa2158df276d0a58249864ad86ac79db",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a29ae027_31c9dfff",
        "filename": "authfs/service/src/authfs.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-04T16:12:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that\u0027s what I mean - we\u0027ll spend time uselessly polling.\nI don\u0027t want to return success if this happens, so we\u0027d end up checking the mountpoint again, and it didn\u0027t seem worth optimizing a case that should never happen.\n(Feel free to remind me when it does ...)",
      "parentUuid": "e0f01337_6849385d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 157,
        "endChar": 37
      },
